Ben: I''m really fond of Impressionism, especially Monet''s garden scenes.
Anna: Why Impressionism? Isn''t it a bit blurry?
Ben: That''s the beauty of it. The painters caught light and feeling, not every detail.
Anna: I see. I prefer modern art myself, like Picasso.
Ben: Picasso? His shapes always confuse me a little.
Anna: Maybe, but he makes me ask a question: what is art, really?
Ben: That''s a great reason. Perhaps we should visit the museum together this weekend.', 'Anna 问 Ben 最喜欢西方艺术哪个时期;Ben 喜欢印象派,尤其莫奈的花园;因为画家捕捉的是光与感觉而非细节;Anna 更喜欢以毕加索为代表的现代艺术;因为它让她思考''艺术是什么'';两人约周末一起去博物馆。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Which art period does Ben like most?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Impressionism.","Modern art.","Primitive art.","The Middle Ages."]},{"q":"Why does Ben like that period?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["It copies every detail.","The painters caught light and feeling.","It uses only black ink.","It is the easiest to draw."]},{"q":"Which kind of art does Anna prefer?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Modern art such as Picasso.","Ink wash painting.","Photography.","Bronze sculpture."]},{"q":"What does Anna say Picasso''s work makes her do?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Fall asleep.","Ask what art really is.","Buy a camera.","Stop visiting museums."]},{"q":"What do they plan to do this weekend?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Paint a garden.","Sell a painting.","Visit a museum together.","Watch a football match."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective3', 'U1');
These films grew out of the old art of ink wash painting.
The most famous one was produced in the 1960s and is still loved today.
Because each frame is hand-painted, the gentle pictures seem to move and breathe.
Sadly, this beautiful style later went into decline because it took so much time and money.', '演讲者介绍中国水墨动画片;它源于古老的水墨画;最著名的一部产生于20世纪60年代,至今仍受喜爱;因为每一帧都是手绘,柔和的画面仿佛会动会呼吸;遗憾的是,这种美丽的风格因耗时耗钱而后来衰落了。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What did ink wash animation films grow out of?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Western photography.","Bronze making.","Modern computer games.","The old art of ink wash painting."]},{"q":"When was the most famous film produced?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["In the 1960s.","In the 1990s.","Last year.","In ancient times."]},{"q":"Why do the pictures seem to move and breathe?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["They are made by machines.","Each frame is hand-painted.","They use bright colours.","They are very short."]},{"q":"Why did this style later go into decline?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["People hated the stories.","It was too colourful.","It took too much time and money.","It was banned by the museum."]},{"q":"How does the speaker feel about this kind of film?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["The speaker finds it boring.","The speaker thinks it is ugly.","The speaker never watches it.","The speaker admires it as a beautiful art."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective3', 'U1');
Visitor: It''s beautiful. Did he really paint the same garden so many times?
Guide: Yes. He was especially fond of the water lilies on his pond.
Visitor: Why did he keep returning to the same scene?
Guide: He wanted to show how the light changed at different times of day.
Visitor: So two paintings of the same pond can look quite different?
Guide: Exactly. Colour and reflection in the water meant everything to him.
Visitor: Now I understand why people call him a master of light.', '讲解员介绍莫奈在吉维尼的著名花园;游客惊叹他多次画同一个花园;讲解员说莫奈尤其喜爱池塘里的睡莲;他反复画同一场景是为表现一天中不同时刻的光线变化;所以同一池塘的两幅画会很不同;色彩与水中倒影对他至关重要;游客明白了为何称他为光的大师。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Whose garden does the room show?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Monet''s.","Picasso''s.","Renoir''s.","Tang Yin''s."]},{"q":"What was Monet especially fond of?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Old bronze bowls.","The water lilies on his pond.","Black-and-white photos.","Tang Dynasty sculptures."]},{"q":"Why did he paint the same scene again and again?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["He had no other ideas.","He was paid to do so.","To show how the light changed through the day.","He could not finish it."]},{"q":"According to the guide, what meant everything to Monet?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Money and fame.","Strict, exact detail.","Religious stories.","Colour and reflection in the water."]},{"q":"What does the visitor finally understand?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Why Monet is called a master of light.","Why the museum is closed.","How to make a camera.","Why ink wash is grey."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective3', 'U1');
Our goal is to display three thousand years of Chinese art under one roof.
The highlight is a snowy mountain painting by the master Tang Yin.
You will also see bronze objects and many Buddhist sculptures.
The show runs until November, and entry is free for children under five.', '欢迎来到美术博物馆的最新展览;我们的目标是在一处呈现中国三千年的艺术;亮点是大师唐寅的一幅雪山图;你还能看到青铜器和许多佛教雕塑;展览持续到十一月,五岁以下儿童免费入场。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is the museum''s goal for this exhibition?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["To sell old cameras.","To display three thousand years of Chinese art.","To teach French painting.","To open a new café."]},{"q":"What is the highlight of the show?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["A modern French film.","An empty white wall.","A snowy mountain painting by Tang Yin.","A box of coins."]},{"q":"What else can visitors see?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only photographs.","Live animals.","Nothing at all.","Bronze objects and Buddhist sculptures."]},{"q":"Until when does the show run?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Until November.","Until next summer.","Only for one day.","It has already closed."]},{"q":"Who can enter the show for free?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Only adults.","Children under five.","Only teachers.","No one at all."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective3', 'U1');
Mr Lee: My advice is to start by copying a work you truly love.
Lily: Won''t that stop me from finding my own style?
Mr Lee: Not at all. Copying first teaches your hand and eye how a master worked.
Lily: I see. What else should I do?
Mr Lee: Paint a little every single day, even if it is only one small thing.
Lily: That sounds hard, but I''ll try my best.
Mr Lee: Don''t worry about being perfect. Step by step, you will surely improve.', 'Lily 想学画却不知如何开始;李老师建议先临摹一幅你真正喜爱的作品;Lily 担心会失去自己的风格;老师说临摹能教会手和眼大师是怎么画的;Lily 又问还该做什么;老师建议每天都画一点,哪怕只是一小样东西;Lily 说有点难但会尽力;老师让她别追求完美,一步步必有进步。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What problem does Lily have?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["She has no money.","She can''t find a museum.","She doesn''t know how to begin painting.","She dislikes art."]},{"q":"What is Mr Lee''s first piece of advice?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Stop painting at once.","Only read books.","Buy expensive paint.","Start by copying a work she loves."]},{"q":"Why does he suggest copying first?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["It teaches the hand and eye how a master worked.","It saves money.","It is easier to sell.","It needs no brush."]},{"q":"What is his second piece of advice?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Never paint alone.","Paint a little every day.","Paint only once a year.","Wait until she is perfect."]},{"q":"What does Mr Lee say will happen step by step?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Lily will give up.","Painting will get harder.","Lily will improve.","Nothing will change."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective3', 'U1');
They no longer wanted only to show the world as it looks.
Some broke objects into shapes; others painted dream-like or abstract scenes.
Their real aim was to make us think about what art can be.
So when a modern painting puzzles you, it is simply inviting you to wonder.', '印象派之后,艺术家开始提出一个大胆的新问题;他们不再只想表现世界本来的样子;有人把物体拆成形状,有人画梦幻或抽象的场景;他们真正的目标是让我们思考艺术可以是什么;所以当一幅现代画让你困惑时,它只是在邀请你去思考。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What did artists begin to do after Impressionism?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Stop painting completely.","Copy photographs exactly.","Only paint gardens.","Ask a brave new question."]},{"q":"What did they no longer want to do?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Only show the world as it looks.","Use any colour.","Visit museums.","Talk to each other."]},{"q":"How did some of these artists paint?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["With only black ink.","In dream-like or abstract scenes.","Exactly like a camera.","Always the same garden."]},{"q":"What was their real aim?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["To earn more money.","To copy old masters.","To make us think about what art can be.","To paint faster."]},{"q":"What does a puzzling modern painting invite you to do?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["To leave at once.","To buy a camera.","To stop looking.","To wonder and think."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective3', 'U1');

